.TH mystrcpy 3 "September 2026" "Version 1.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int mystrcpy(char *dest, const char *src);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBmystrcpy\fR function copies the string pointed to by \fBsrc\fR, including the terminating null byte, to the buffer pointed to by \fBdest\fR. It returns 0 on success, or -1 if either pointer is NULL.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Abdur Rehman
